hermes v0.23.0: model_catalog.openrouter_exclude_native keeps OpenRouter off
models the agent can reach through their own vendor's provider.

Claude via OpenRouter costs far more than the same model through the
`anthropic` provider (TeamClaude). An agent once set
`delegation.provider: openrouter` + `delegation.model:
anthropic/claude-opus-5.5` itself (`hermes config set`) and every subagent
billed OpenRouter. With `model_catalog.openrouter_exclude_native:
[anthropic]` and a working Anthropic credential:

- catalog: OpenRouter's anthropic/* rows leave fetch_openrouter_models
  (so model_ids, provider_model_ids, /api/model/options, TUI and messaging
  /model, `hermes model`) and drop_unofferable_model_ids filters the
  openrouter picker row; the state is part of _credential_fingerprint
  ("openrouter") so provider_models_cache.json follows the credential;
- resolution: an OpenRouter request for such a model is REWRITTEN to the
  native provider with the same model (anthropic/claude-opus-5.5 ->
  claude-opus-5-5) and logged as a WARNING at each chokepoint:
  resolve_runtime_provider (main model, delegation.provider, cron jobs),
  delegate_tool_config._resolve_child_runtime (delegate_task children,
  delegation routes, inherited OpenRouter parents with a model override),
  init_agent (backstop for every AIAgent constructor, plus its fallback
  chain), agent switch_model and model_switch.switch_model (/model),
  bind_route_entry (fallback activation), resolve_provider_client and
  the auxiliary OpenRouter lane.

"OpenRouter" = provider openrouter, any base_url at openrouter.ai, or a
named custom provider whose configured base_url is (is_openrouter_route).
Only provider+model pairs are rewritten: a model-less
resolve_runtime_provider(requested="openrouter") (image_gen/video_gen
openrouter plugins, account_usage credits) and any call with an explicit
api_key/base_url keep OpenRouter's key and URL; without a target_model,
model.default counts only for the main runtime (requested unset/"auto")
and only when model.provider is itself OpenRouter.
An agent already on anthropic whose model string is an OpenRouter id
(gateway, cron and CLI build the main agent from model.default) gets the
same id mapping in init_agent/switch_model (native_id_fixup).

Ids: a `:<variant>` suffix (:thinking, :beta, :nitro, :floor, :extended)
is dropped; `-fast` ids (anthropic/claude-opus-5-fast) run the base model
with {"speed": "fast"} request overrides where the base model accepts
fast mode (agent.model_metadata), for that model only: the agent records
the route (_native_fast_route) and effective_request_overrides drops the
speed on any other model (fallback activation, /model), and never sends
speed to a non-Anthropic-messages wire or a model without fast mode; `~anthropic/...-latest` aliases and
undated short ids resolve through _PROVIDER_MODELS["anthropic"] (exact id,
else its newest dated snapshot, else for -latest the newest listed id of
that family); otherwise the plain normalized id, logged.

"Working credential" = resolve_runtime_provider(requested=<vendor>)
returns that provider with a key (cached 60 s per HERMES_HOME). Without
it, nothing changes: agents with only an OpenRouter key keep its Claude.
Unset/empty (the default): upstream behaviour.

Tests: no upstream pytest file ships with this patch; the offline check
hyperhermes/checks/openrouter-native runs the assertions against the
built package.

Upstream status: not reported; hyperhermes-only option.

